rec(648,2019,[15,11,6,9,8,8,7,3,2.5,1.5],0,0,'The financial analogy supplies a continuous conceptual journey into gauge theory and geometry. The expert/explanatory exception admits that sustained account; course use and derivations alone are not sufficient to exclude it.','The account uses established mathematics and physics; analogical shortcuts need care and the author’s standing is below a specialist monograph’s.|Gauge freedom, geometry and financial exchange are connected, giving a useful modeling analogy, though little new strategic payload for a QFT expert.|A short focused account earns its length; the geometric concepts remain durable.|The intuitive sequence is readable but an analogy cannot carry every technical distinction.',{evidence:['https://play.google.com/store/books/details/Jakob_Schwichtenberg_Physics_from_Finance?id=kBaVDwAAQBAJ'],yearNote:'Publisher-supplied record gives first release in February 2019.'});
rec(660,2003,[19,11,8,11,9,9,7,5,2.5,2],0,0,'The authors’ foreword explicitly organizes the sequence around the organic unity of analysis and its links to other mathematics and science. That sustained conceptual narrative qualifies under the revised expert exception, even though the books originated in courses.','Established proofs and the authors’ specialist authority support high integrity; technical scope is clearly delimited.|Fourier, complex, real and functional analysis are linked through common ideas and applications; the synthesis supports transferable modeling habits rather than direct institutional strategy.|The dense progression earns its technical length and the mathematical material is durable.|The motivating cross-volume story is coherent and the formal prose exact.',{yearNote:'The first volume Fourier Analysis appeared in 2003; that year applies to the nominated series, not the final 2011 volume.',evidence:['https://assets.press.princeton.edu/chapters/s7562.pdf']});
rec(664,2001,[19,8,7,11,9,9,7,5,2,2],0,0,'Varadhan develops probability from foundations to limit behavior as a connected conceptual account. Its concise graduate-course origin no longer suffices for exclusion where the expert explanation is sustained and no exam or operating-manual purpose is shown.','Rigorous probability arguments and Varadhan’s research authority support high integrity.|Measure, independence, convergence and limit laws connect internally; probabilistic abstraction transfers well but cross-institution integration is limited.|The concise technical treatment is dense and durable.|The logical progression is precise but assumes a strong mathematical reader.',{evidence:['https://www.ams.org/publications/authors/books/postpub/author-pages-test'],yearNote:'AMS lists the original Courant Lecture Notes volume 7 in 2001.'});
rec(683,2014,[18,10,7,10,8,9,7,4.5,3,1.5],0,0,'Lancaster and Blundell build a sustained explanatory journey into fields, symmetries and particles, with motivation beyond a sequence of exam techniques. The revised expert exception admits that narrative; the previous course/self-study label is not decisive.','Established field-theory material and academic authorship support reliability; pedagogical simplifications limit precision relative to research texts.|Field, symmetry, particles and condensed-matter ideas connect, but the incremental strategic utility for an existing QFT specialist is modest.|The explanatory length is largely earned and foundational ideas endure.|The accessible narrative is coherent, with deliberate technical simplification.',{yearNote:'Oxford’s original edition is 2014; later paperback dates do not reset age.',evidence:['https://academic.oup.com/book/36442']});
rec(684,2014,[18,8,6,9,8,9,7,5,3,1.5],0,0,'The development of quantum states, measurement and dynamics is a sustained conceptual explanation for a technically capable reader. Course compatibility and exercises alone do not override the revised expert narrative exception.','The account rests on established quantum mechanics and Susskind’s authority; it deliberately simplifies the formal landscape.|State spaces, operators, measurement and entanglement connect clearly; transfer is mainly conceptual and adds limited novelty for a theoretical physicist.|The compact progression earns its length and basic quantum structure is durable.|Clear conceptual sequencing is a strength, with some precision traded for accessibility.',{yearNote:'The quantum-mechanics volume first appeared in 2014; it is distinct from the 2013 mechanics volume.'});
rec(685,2013,[19,10,7,11,8,9,7,5,2.5,2],0,0,'Hall explains quantum mechanics to mathematicians through a connected account of its mathematical and physical structures. That cross-field explanatory purpose and conversational development meet the revised expert exception despite use as a course text.','Detailed mathematical arguments and specialist authorship support high integrity.|Functional analysis, classical structures and quantum theory are connected; modeling transfer is good but direct institutional strategy is limited.|The extensive rigorous treatment is substantially earned and foundational material durable.|The cumulative exposition is readable for its intended expert audience and mathematically precise.',{yearConfidence:'high',yearNote:'Springer records the original edition in 2013.',evidence:['https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4614-7116-5']});
rec(698,2005,[19,9,7,11,9,9,7,5,2.5,2],0,0,'This volume links measure, integration and Hilbert spaces through a cumulative explanatory account. It shares the series’ explicit unity-of-analysis narrative, which the updated expert exception admits independently of classroom use.','Established analysis with careful proofs and strong author authority supports high integrity.|Measure, integration and Hilbert-space structure connect; abstract modeling habits transfer, while industrial or institutional links remain indirect.|Dense development earns its length and is mathematically durable.|The conceptual progression is coherent and the definitions precise.',{yearNote:'The separately nominated Real Analysis volume first appeared in 2005, distinct from the series start in 2003.'});
rec(773,2017,[18,10,6,10,8,9,7,5,3,1.5],0,0,'Susskind and Friedman explain the route from relativity to fields through a motivated conceptual sequence. That narrative meets the revised expert exception; self-study calculations and exercises alone are no longer decisive exclusions.','Established relativistic and field-theoretic material and Susskind’s expertise support reliability, with pedagogical simplifications.|Symmetry, spacetime, electromagnetism and fields connect, but the user’s existing QFT training limits incremental utility.|Focused development is dense enough and the theoretical foundations endure.|The conceptual arc is readable and carefully explained, though not at research-monograph precision.',{yearNote:'The relativity and field-theory volume first appeared in 2017.'});
rec(902,2005,[17,13,11,10,8,8,4,5,2.5,2],0,-10,'Armendáriz and Morduch integrate theory, field evidence, institutions and incentives in a sustained explanation of microfinance. The explicit conceptual and empirical account passes the revised expert exception despite its teaching use.','Economic research and field evidence support the account; causal impact remains difficult to identify and is treated as an empirical question.|Credit constraints, information, group incentives, savings and institutions connect strongly; incentive design lessons transfer beyond microfinance.|The technical length is substantially earned; some empirical detail dates but information and incentive constraints persist.|The argument is cumulative and precise, with mathematical demands.',{author:'Beatriz Armendáriz; Jonathan Morduch',yearNote:'The original first edition appeared in 2005; the publisher’s second edition is 2010.',evidence:['https://mitpress.ublish.com/book/economics-microfinance'],themeNote:'Finance and lending are central, so T12=-10. Gender and poverty applications do not make racial/civil-movement or single-nation history predominant.'});
rec(1006,2006,[18,12,10,10,8,9,6,4,2.5,2],0,-10,'The book develops a connected mathematical explanation of voting, representation and strategic interaction. That cross-field explanatory structure qualifies under the revised exception; course use and exercises alone do not retain H2.','Mathematical models and proofs support reliable conditional conclusions; institutional assumptions limit empirical generalization.|Voting rules, apportionment, choice and games connect mathematics to institutional design; tradeoff reasoning transfers broadly.|A focused formal treatment earns its length and the structural constraints endure.|The cumulative mathematical account is clear and disciplined.',{yearNote:'The original edition is 2006; later editions expand the same work.',themeNote:'Political decision systems are central, so T12=-10; no T11 theme predominates.'});
rec(1055,2009,[19,10,7,11,8,9,7,5,2.5,2],0,0,'Vakil explicitly builds a motivated mathematical story connecting nearby fields and explaining why the central ideas fit together. That sustained expert exposition meets the revised exception; its course designation and interspersed exercises do not by themselves justify H2.','Rigorous algebraic geometry and the author’s direct research authority support high integrity; a developing manuscript can contain corrigible details.|Algebra, geometry, topology and categorical thinking connect strongly inside mathematics; abstraction transfers but practical strategy is indirect.|The very long treatment is mostly earned by explanations and examples, with a modest density reduction; foundations are durable.|The motivating voice and cumulative path support narrative clarity while retaining precise formal definitions.',{yearConfidence:'moderate',yearNote:'Use 2009 for the identifiable consolidated Foundations of Algebraic Geometry course-note work, documented on the author’s 2009–10 page. Earlier 2005–08 course notes are precursors; the later 2024 copyright and print publication do not reset this manuscript’s production age.',evidence:['https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/0910-216/','https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/0910-216/FOAGevolution.html','https://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/216blog/FOAGjul2724public.pdf']});
rec(1097,2013,[18,10,6,10,8,9,7,5,3,1.5],0,0,'The nominated series offers a connected conceptual route through theoretical physics for a technically capable general reader. The revised expert/narrative exception admits this sustained explanation; a self-study course designation alone is insufficient for exclusion.','Established physics and Susskind’s expertise support reliability, though the series deliberately compresses advanced qualifications.|Mechanics, quantum theory, relativity and fields are connected; the main limitation is low incremental utility for a QFT specialist.|The focused conceptual treatment is largely earned and foundational ideas remain durable.|The progression is unusually readable for technical physics, at some cost to exhaustive formal detail.',{yearNote:'The series begins with the 2013 mechanics volume; later volumes do not reset the series original year.'});
rec(1098,2013,[18,8,6,9,8,9,7,5,3,1.5],0,0,'The first volume develops mechanics and its mathematical language through a sustained conceptual narrative. The updated expert exception applies even though the reader can use it for self-study; it is not exam preparation or a machine-operation manual.','The mechanics is established and the author has direct theoretical authority; accessibility requires some compression.|State, motion, conservation and variational thinking connect; their modeling habits transfer but add limited novelty for an advanced physicist.|The concise development earns its length and classical foundations are durable.|The conceptual arc is clear, memorable and reasonably precise.',{yearNote:'The mechanics volume first appeared in 2013, also the start year of the separately nominated series.'});
